{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Every, done</b> — [bet–gimel] two joined." "<b>Meaning:</b> Every way of a man is straight in his eyes — HaShem sees, and He weighs hearts, to do His will. Therefore we know, and His eyes are a hint to His understanding, and the act of righteousness and justice — it is chosen for Him over the altar."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {1 "The phrase 'ועיניו רמז לשכלו' is textually uncertain; translated hyper-literally. The referent of 'we know' (והוא תוכן לבות / וידענו) may shift between man and God, but the syntax is preserved as found."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:56.092699390Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}